cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Closed-loop fault dataset and detection for DC motor drives"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Vásquez Castro"
    given-names: "Néstor Oswaldo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-6483-790X"
    affiliation: "Universidad Central, Bogotá, Colombia"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/nvasquezc/dc-motor-fault-detection"
abstract: >
  Embedded acquisition and analysis platform for DC motor drives operating
  under closed-loop control. Angular speed and input-referred disturbance
  are jointly estimated on an ARM Cortex-M4 using a Kalman filter, enabling
  fault signatures to be recorded under the feedback conditions in which
  real drives operate. Fault severity is parameterized in physical units so
  that detection thresholds transfer across test benches.
keywords:
  - DC motor
  - Kalman filter
  - fault detection
  - predictive maintenance
  - embedded systems
  - STM32